Priority: 1
Area: Canvas
Status: done
Depends on: add-text-tool

Goal:
Fix the first-pass text tool so a normal click reliably opens text entry and allows the user to type visible text onto the canvas.

Context:
The initial text tool added the editor on pointer-down. In practice that can collapse the editor before typing begins, especially in desktop-webview click sequences where focus changes complete after pointer-up.

Expected changes:

- move text-editor creation to a stable completed-click point
- preserve the existing commit flow of blur or Ctrl+Enter / Cmd+Enter
- keep text placement local to Canvas Mode without widening into re-edit or rich-text work

Acceptance criteria:

- Selecting the Text tool and clicking the canvas opens a visible editor that stays open long enough to type.
- Typing text and blurring or confirming commits a visible text item to the canvas.
- Empty clicks still fail closed without creating empty text items.

Notes:

- Keep the fix narrow and interaction-focused.
- Re-editing existing text is still out of scope for this repair slice.
